The 34th Richard G. McSpadden Report has been modernized to reflect changes in industry standards. While accident counts remain, the classification system used to denote phase and accident cause has changed. This effort standardizes data with current NTSB reporting and creates future opportunity for wider applications within the AOPA Air Safety Institute.

